{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01542",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.76,
      "end_seconds": 4.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.72,
      "end_seconds": 8.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.37,
      "end_seconds": 18.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Mainly swollen legs by evening. There's a a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.1,
      "end_seconds": 24.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "So, has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.93,
      "end_seconds": 36.26,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.72,
      "end_seconds": 41.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.85,
      "end_seconds": 44.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "about a four out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.95,
      "end_seconds": 47.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Anything that improves it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.82,
      "end_seconds": 52.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Only feet up, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.03,
      "end_seconds": 56.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.66,
      "end_seconds": 60.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "It's once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.36,
      "end_seconds": 63.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Has there been aching legs too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.31,
      "end_seconds": 79.4,
      "duration_seconds": 14.09,
      "text": "yes, uh, actually oh, and a sore on my ankle that won't heal with sore on my ankle that won't heal, only elevation, and it's not much"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.35,
      "end_seconds": 86.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "and what about spreading redness, calf pain, chest pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.42,
      "end_seconds": 90.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.24,
      "end_seconds": 92.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.43,
      "end_seconds": 96.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.56,
      "end_seconds": 100.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.53,
      "end_seconds": 103.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.62,
      "end_seconds": 122.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Okay, how are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.05,
      "end_seconds": 132.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.16,
      "end_seconds": 137.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.37,
      "end_seconds": 141.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.48,
      "end_seconds": 145.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.19,
      "end_seconds": 162.03,
      "duration_seconds": 15.84,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler, once a day. I'm on carbamazepine, 200 milligrams, twice a day. Though honestly, some days I forget to take it. I was on levetiracetam before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.87,
      "end_seconds": 165.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.77,
      "end_seconds": 183.29,
      "duration_seconds": 16.52,
      "text": "I have COPD, for about a year. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I've got epilepsy. I'm not great at remembering details, so so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.26,
      "end_seconds": 185.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.49,
      "end_seconds": 192.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "right, so epilepsy is already on your record we'll keep that in mind today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.41,
      "end_seconds": 205.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.19,
      "end_seconds": 213.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.92,
      "end_seconds": 234.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.8 degrees, blood pressure 111 over 80, SpO2 97 percent on room air. And respiratory rate 15, heart rate 84."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.06,
      "end_seconds": 237.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "is that that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.79,
      "end_seconds": 241.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.36,
      "end_seconds": 245.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.53,
      "end_seconds": 249.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.02,
      "end_seconds": 265.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "There is a shallow ulcer above the inner ankle with brown skin around it and visible varicose veins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.21,
      "end_seconds": 271.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.57,
      "end_seconds": 288.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "right, here's what I'm thinking it points towards a venous leg ulcer another possibility is an arterial ulcer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.55,
      "end_seconds": 291.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.48,
      "end_seconds": 310.26,
      "duration_seconds": 17.78,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a venous leg ulcer is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had swollen legs by evening, and no chest pain or spreading redness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.01,
      "end_seconds": 311.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.33,
      "end_seconds": 320.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "We should do a wound swab for leg ulcer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 321.66,
      "end_seconds": 326.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "We have a slot Wednesday at 10 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.33,
      "end_seconds": 358.82,
      "duration_seconds": 30.49,
      "text": "I want a doppler test of the leg pulses done, that's for leg ulcer. Compression bandaging and keeping the leg raised when sitting. Don't skip meals, and and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. Come back in two weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.46,
      "end_seconds": 366.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.08,
      "end_seconds": 369.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}